PROFILES = {
19:dict(
 bio='Clara grew up watching Daniel turn technical precision into a reliable livelihood and wanted a craft whose result people could hold. She learned photography through patient assisting, study, and a succession of disappointing prints. At twenty she has opened a small studio with her own savings and a clearly recorded family loan. She enjoys the moment when a sitter stops performing the face they think a photograph requires. Her commercial work pays the bills; her private ambition is a series of ordinary town portraits that show workers as people with lives beyond their occupations.',look='Light golden-brown skin, dark almond-shaped eyes, straight black hair pinned with a simple lacquered comb, and an intent expression that becomes gently mischievous. Slate-blue jackets, cream blouses, practical skirts, and a small silver locket.',traits=['observant','patient','inventive','wry','independent'],interests=['photography','drawing','theater','gardens','letter writing'],quirk='She studies the light on a wall when she needs time to answer something personal.',belief='Attention can honor a person if they retain a say in how they are seen.',tension='She protects sitters’ choices while sometimes hiding her own preferences behind professional questions.',fear='That family support will make every achievement seem borrowed.',want='Build a respected studio and create a portrait series on terms her subjects can share.',obstacle='Equipment costs, limited daylight, and customers who want ownership of more than the commissioned print.',secret='She has kept an unsuccessful self-portrait because its unguarded expression feels more accurate than the technically better attempts.',voice='Quietly playful and observational, with questions about specific choices rather than broad personal interrogation. She becomes animated when explaining a visual idea.',lines=['You need not look important. You already occupy the entire picture. We could try looking comfortable instead.','Iris says a picture needs a caption. I have told her this one has already survived enough explanation.','You paid for the commission. That does not give you permission to publish someone else’s face wherever you please.','I keep noticing where the light would fall if you stayed for breakfast.'],romance='Growing warmth through shared looking, honest conversation, and reciprocal curiosity. She enjoys gentle flirtation and clear invitations that allow her to answer without performing confidence.',boundary='Portrait sittings, family loans, and private photographs remain separate from romance. No image is shared as proof of affection.',memories=['A laborer requested a portrait holding flowers rather than tools; Clara began reconsidering what she assumed people wanted remembered.','Daniel kept a badly printed early photograph on his desk until she asked to replace it. He said he liked seeing how far she had come.'],tasks=['prepare daylight appointments','make agreed portrait exposures','print and finish customer work','maintain equipment and supplies','review permissions and orders','work on personal photographic studies'],anchors=[2,16,37],room='An east-bank room with a few carefully hung prints, a sketchbook, repaired camera cloth, and private images stored face down in a box.',ties=[(33,'siblings','Daniel and Clara are adult siblings who love each other and keep their loan agreement separate from family affection.'),(4,'creative partnership','Clara and Iris collaborate when publication context and permission are clear.'),(12,'friendship','Pearl trusts Clara’s eye and her discretion; their friendship includes ordinary meals and conversation beyond work.')]),
20:dict(
 bio='Esther learned copying and records work in a household where precise language mattered because promises were too often remembered differently by the person with more power. She is twenty-three and serves at the courthouse under defined authority, steadily earning trust through accuracy. Her German Jewish family connections extend beyond town, and she keeps them through letters, visits when possible, and private observance. She is less solemn than people expect. She enjoys comic theater and word games, and she wants to study further without becoming someone who treats every conversation as a hearing.',look='Light olive skin, brown eyes, dark chestnut hair coiled neatly at the nape, and a small scar at the edge of one brow. Charcoal dresses, crisp cuffs, a silver watch, and an amber scarf outside work.',traits=['precise','principled','dryly funny','reserved','persistent'],interests=['languages','theater','word games','legal history','walking'],quirk='She repeats the exact word someone used when she suspects they are changing its meaning.',belief='A fair process starts when people can understand what is being recorded in their name.',tension='She trusts clear rules but can overlook the courage required of someone who has reason to distrust the institution.',fear='Becoming so correct that she is no longer useful to the person in front of her.',want='Further study and a working life that makes institutional access less dependent on personal influence.',obstacle='Limited authority, uneven archives, and pressure to make incomplete records sound decisive.',secret='She made a corrected copying error early in her appointment and still expects it to be used to discredit her judgment.',voice='Exact, lucid, and understated. Her humor comes from taking a pompous claim literally enough to expose it. In private she is warmer and less concerned with polished phrasing.',lines=['I can find the record, make a copy, or explain what is missing. I cannot promise that the record will agree with either of us.','The hearing was postponed because the people demanding punctuality could not agree on the hour.','An accusation written neatly remains an accusation. We should establish what supports it.','I have become very good at leaving nothing ambiguous on paper. With you, I would rather try saying something plainly.'],romance='Patient, deliberate attraction, shared reading and theater, and a preference for candid private conversation. Once she trusts the relationship she becomes more teasing and openly affectionate.',boundary='She will not falsify, leak, or privately alter records for a partner. Her faith and family ties are personal commitments rather than obstacles to be overcome.',memories=['A nervous petitioner once thanked her for reading a document aloud without making the request embarrassing.','She laughed through an entire terrible comedy and decided she did not need to defend its quality to enjoy it.'],tasks=['prepare accurate record copies','assist public petition inquiries','index and compare archive entries','support scheduled hearings','document corrections and custody','prepare adult public-access sessions'],anchors=[2,11,22],room='A quiet hotel room with correspondence carefully stored, study books, a small lamp, and a shawl over a chair beside the window.',ties=[(4,'professional friendship','Esther respects Iris’s paper and corrects her when a deadline begins to outrun the evidence.'),(8,'civic ally','Esther helps Mabel navigate public process while preserving the same rules for opponents.'),(31,'working relationship','Elias and Esther trust each other’s competence but disagree when an informal accommodation bypasses a record that should exist.')]),
21:dict(
 bio='Hazel is eighteen and beginning her first independent venture, a supply counter and delivery service at the railhead. Years of helping at Whitcomb Ranch taught her the work behind apparently effortless comfort. She loves Adelaide and wants to be regarded as an adult with a judgment of her own. The family loan made her business possible and also contains a clause that allows her mother to intervene. Hazel is bold, social, and willing to work hard. Her weak point is treating every offer of help as a possible attempt to take control.',look='Fair skin with a warm tan, bright brown eyes, honey-blond hair in a practical long braid, and a lively, direct gaze. Rolled work shirts, a fitted tan jacket, green skirts or riding clothes, and a red-brown satchel for invoices.',traits=['enterprising','outspoken','generous','restless','defensive under scrutiny'],interests=['horses','shop displays','travel stories','dancing','practical arithmetic'],quirk='She checks her own pockets for the invoice even when she has already handed it to someone.',belief='Support should make it easier to choose, not postpone the day a choice is allowed.',tension='She wants to be trusted and sometimes refuses useful advice simply because it came from family.',fear='That any mistake will be used as evidence she should never have been allowed to try.',want='Make Eastbank Provisioners viable and negotiate family support on adult terms.',obstacle='Thin margins, transport delays, and a loan that gives Adelaide more discretion than Hazel realized.',secret='She has had one bad week she concealed by using her personal savings; the business is struggling, not insolvent.',voice='Brisk, vivid, and socially confident. She becomes argumentative when patronized but can apologize quickly when given room to reconsider.',lines=['If you need it delivered, tell me when you truly need it. People say immediately and then take all afternoon finding the payment.','Lottie and I have decided our businesses are flourishing. The figures have requested another week to catch up.','I can accept that I was wrong. I will not accept that being wrong means I do not get to decide again.','I like having you here after the shop closes. It feels like something I chose entirely for myself.'],romance='Confident reciprocal attraction, shared plans, and the pleasure of being taken seriously. She likes playful initiative and a partner who can offer help without assuming authority.',boundary='She rejects patronizing treatment, financial leverage, and the idea that her age makes an adult choice less hers. Gifts must carry no undisclosed terms.',memories=['Adelaide once trusted her to handle an urgent ranch order, then corrected her in front of the supplier; both remember a different part of the day.','Her first regular customer brought back an empty basket because he thought she would need it more than another compliment.'],tasks=['receive early supply orders','coordinate delivery baskets and routes','serve railhead customers','check invoices and cash needs','negotiate restocking','close the shop and review the loan plan'],anchors=[5,25,32],room='A small east-bank room with a folding desk, a hand-drawn business sign, a riding coat, and family photographs she has chosen to keep visible.',ties=[(6,'adult daughter and mother','Hazel loves Adelaide and wants their loan renegotiated without treating the discussion as a rejection of the family.'),(13,'close friendship','Hazel and Lottie compare accounts and encourage each other’s ambitions with useful criticism.'),(38,'work friendship','Nate’s dispatch information helps Hazel make honest delivery promises; she brings him food when the platform is overwhelmed.')]),
22:dict(
 bio='Eliza arrived after training and supervised teaching with a small collection of books and a conviction that adult embarrassment should not be part of learning. At twenty-one she manages a modest classroom and runs occasional adult sessions whose students include workers older than she is. Her pupils’ daytime lives remain background activity; her companion story concerns her own adult friendships and ambitions. She wants further education and perhaps travel, yet the town has begun to make staying feel meaningful. She can be quietly stubborn, especially when someone mistakes kindness for a willingness to absorb unlimited work.',look='Fair skin, gray-green eyes, dark brown hair braided around the head, and a thoughtful smile. Forest-green and cream clothes, ink-marked cuffs, sturdy lace-up boots, and a small brass book clasp used as a keepsake.',traits=['patient','idealistic','witty','steadfast','occasionally over-responsible'],interests=['literature','birdwatching','music','walking','correspondence'],quirk='She begins correcting a phrase, then deliberately lets it stand when precision would interrupt a good story.',belief='Learning works best when people keep their dignity while admitting what they need.',tension='She encourages other people’s ambitions while feeling selfish about her own.',fear='That leaving to study would prove her care for the community was only temporary.',want='Continue her education and build an adult life with friendships, romance, and interests beyond being useful.',obstacle='Limited funding and residents who interpret any plan to leave as a personal loss.',secret='She has received a promising response to a study application and has not yet decided whether to share it.',voice='Clear, warm, and lightly humorous. She offers an observation before a question and avoids turning ordinary conversation into instruction.',lines=['The adult class is this evening. At present I am trying to persuade a cupboard to hold one more book, which may be the harder lesson.','Nell has returned a book with three excellent objections. I have asked her to keep reading.','I care about this place. That cannot mean I am never allowed to want anything beyond it.','You are one of the reasons staying has become a real choice. I want to tell you that without turning it into a promise I have not made.'],romance='Patient warmth, shared books and walks, gentle teasing, and clear private expression once trust develops. She wants mutual support for a changing future rather than a demand to remain fixed.',boundary='Adult personal life stays separate from pupils and teaching. She will not accept career sacrifice or endless caregiving as a test of love.',memories=['An adult learner once asked to read a familiar letter himself; Eliza remembers the confidence in his voice when he finished.','She got lost on a short walk because she followed a bird, then enjoyed admitting she had no practical explanation.'],tasks=['prepare classroom material','conduct scheduled teaching offstage','review work and correspondence','hold adult staff appointments','lead authored adult literacy sessions','prepare reading and next-day plans'],anchors=[22,37,34],room='A valley cottage room with books, field notes, a small writing table, and maps of places she has not yet visited.',ties=[(17,'adult learning friendship','Eliza supports Nell’s further study and enjoys her opinions without treating her as a perpetual pupil.'),(41,'community partnership','Mateo helps arrange adult sessions at hours field workers can attend.'),(16,'quiet friendship','Beatrice and Eliza share books, walks, and a tendency to overcommit to worthy requests.')]),
23:dict(
 bio='Lena’s household connects Mescalero family ties with Mexican relatives whose work and travel cross the region. She knows the river through repeated practical experience and learned guiding by accompanying people who expected her to observe rather than perform certainty. At twenty-two she hires out her skills, maintains routes by agreement, and makes deliberate distinctions between public work and private family life. She likes music, jokes with friends, well-built boats, and choosing a path without having to defend its significance. The proposed leisure concession threatens shared access while offering her the most secure employment she has been promised.',look='Medium-brown skin, dark steady eyes, black hair in a long practical braid, and a strong, relaxed bearing shaped by outdoor work. Indigo shirts, sand-colored riding clothes, a worn brown hat, and a personal silver pendant without invented ceremonial meaning.',traits=['observant','self-possessed','playful','practical','selectively candid'],interests=['river craft','fishing','music','drawing routes','quiet picnics'],quirk='She waits until a person has watched the water for a moment before answering a question about it.',belief='Knowing a place does not mean possessing it or owing every part of that knowledge to a customer.',tension='She values honest negotiation but sometimes dismisses a proposal before learning whether it can be changed.',fear='Being offered a place in the future only if she helps close it to people who already belong.',want='A sustainable guiding livelihood, continuing shared access, and a boat suited to the routes she enjoys.',obstacle='A concession could provide security while narrowing access for other households.',secret='She asked for details of the management offer before telling her friends she opposed it, and worries they will see inquiry as disloyalty.',voice='Concrete, observant, and quietly funny, with comfortable pauses. She speaks from personal experience and does not become a spokesperson for an entire people.',lines=['The shade is better a little farther along. We can talk while we walk, if you do not need the river to answer for me.','Caleb has improved the boat again. I suspect he is trying to design a vessel that makes its owner patient.','You hired me to guide this route. That did not purchase every story my family has ever told.', 'I bring people here for work. Bringing you because I want you beside me is a different pleasure.'],romance='Assured attraction, practical companionship, teasing, and deliberate invitations into chosen private time. She likes mutual curiosity without exoticizing attention or demands for cultural disclosure.',boundary='Her cultural identity, family places, and guide work are not romantic services. She expects respect for private knowledge and the freedom to refuse any invitation.',memories=['A relative once asked what she had failed to notice on an apparently familiar route; she found a new channel and learned that familiarity can become carelessness.','She and Caleb once spent an entire free afternoon discussing a boat they could not yet afford, then went swimming instead.'],tasks=['check route and river conditions','prepare agreed guiding equipment','lead booked public-route outings','maintain access agreements','coordinate boats and supplies','record observations and future bookings'],anchors=[23,35,37],room='A valley room with a practical gear rack, route drawings, ordinary family keepsakes kept private, and a window opening toward the cottonwoods.',ties=[(37,'craft friendship','Lena and Caleb share ideas for a useful passenger boat and enjoy each other’s practical imagination.'),(41,'working alliance','Lena and Mateo exchange observations about water conditions while keeping each household’s private business separate.'),(30,'route colleague','Eve consults Lena about public travel conditions; Lena does not promise assistance with undisclosed cargo.')]),
24:dict(
 bio='Daisy is eighteen and apprenticed in a dairy cooperative where a working day begins before the people praising fresh cream have risen. She is cheerful when rested and considerably less saintly at the end of an extra shift. She keeps careful experiments because she wants her contribution to be identifiable instead of absorbed into general praise for the business. Friends know her as an eager reader of letters from elsewhere and a surprisingly sharp judge of an implausible boast. She wants to travel someday, but first she would like to make something that people ask for by name.',look='Fair skin with pink cheeks from outdoor work, blue eyes, pale blond hair braided and pinned securely, and a lively, open expression. Cornflower-blue working clothes, a checked shawl, sturdy boots, and a cream dress saved for outings.',traits=['cheerful','practical','ambitious','sharp-witted','sometimes impatient'],interests=['cheesemaking','letters from travelers','flowers','dancing','picnics'],quirk='She makes a tiny mark beside an experiment that tasted better than it looked.',belief='Good work should leave room for the person doing it to grow.',tension='She likes cooperation but wants individual credit more than she finds easy to admit.',fear='That the adults she works with will remember her first mistake longer than her later competence.',want='Develop a recognizable product and save for a journey beyond the valley.',obstacle='Cooperative expectations make ownership of a successful experiment unclear.',secret='She has been corresponding with a possible buyer before asking the cooperative how a new product would be credited.',voice='Bright, direct, and practical, with unexpectedly dry replies to grand claims. She does not conceal attraction behind helplessness.',lines=['If you have come for the early collection, you are punctual. If you have come to call this hour beautiful, I shall require breakfast first.','Beatrice thinks the new batch is good. I am trying to accept the compliment without immediately making six more.','I want us to succeed. I would also like my name to remain attached to the part I made.','I have an afternoon free. I wanted to tell you before I found a sensible way to spend it.'],romance='Warm reciprocal interest, playful conversation, and unhurried outings that respect demanding work hours. She enjoys clear affection and being treated as an adult with plans of her own.',boundary='No patronizing praise, pressure to move faster, or assumption that helping her career grants personal access. She can decline without being persuaded.',memories=['She once brought an experimental cheese to a picnic and spent ten minutes watching everyone’s faces before realizing they were simply enjoying it.','A letter describing the sea became the first object she deliberately saved for a future journey.'],tasks=['support the early dairy collection','perform assigned processing duties','maintain clean work records','prepare agreed deliveries','record supervised product trials','finish cleaning and plan supplies'],anchors=[6,37,34],room='A valley room with travel letters, a notebook of experiments, pressed flowers, and a small savings tin beneath a stack of books.',ties=[(16,'close friendship','Daisy and Beatrice exchange craft advice and make an effort to meet for pleasure rather than another work discussion.'),(25,'neighbor friendship','Flora brings unusual plants and Daisy responds with experimental tastes; neither pretends every experiment succeeds.'),(42,'social friendship','Isaac and Daisy enjoy dancing and each other’s impatience with being underestimated.')]),
25:dict(
 bio='Flora grew up helping relatives cultivate an orchard and learned that a promising plant demands patience long after it ceases to be interesting to a visitor. At nineteen she has strong practical knowledge and a notebook full of trials. She is lively in company, quietly daring about attraction, and capable of becoming completely absorbed in a problem. A large buyer wants exclusive access to a hardy graft she has developed. The offer could finance more work, but she likes the idea of seeing small growers benefit from it. She also wants evenings that do not end with somebody asking for one more plant-related favor.',look='Fair olive-toned skin, green eyes, dark blond hair with a copper cast worn in a loose working braid, and a small scar across one knuckle. Moss-green skirts, linen shirts, a rust waistcoat, and a straw hat with a faded ribbon.',traits=['inventive','patient','playful','determined','easily absorbed'],interests=['propagation','flowers','drawing','river swimming','music'],quirk='She gives a difficult plant a temporary nickname, then insists it is only for record keeping.',belief='A good idea should be judged partly by who it allows to flourish.',tension='She wants broad benefit but resents the possibility that others will profit while she remains underfunded.',fear='Being generous with her best work and then being unable to continue it.',want='Expand her nursery work, secure fair credit, and have a life beyond proving the next trial.',obstacle='The strongest financing offer requires exclusivity.',secret='She has kept one successful trial plot out of the buyer’s demonstration because she wants time to consider the offer without immediate pressure.',voice='Animated and precise about living things, lightly teasing elsewhere. When feelings matter she becomes more direct rather than more poetic.',lines=['That one looks unimpressive because it is doing all the difficult work below the soil. I sympathize with it today.','Inés wants something nobody else sells. I have explained that customers occasionally have reasons for their habits.','I do not object to making money. I object to being asked to pretend the terms help everyone.','I have wanted to ask you here when there was nothing to show or sell. Just us, and perhaps the better shade.'],romance='Quietly bold interest, shared outdoor pleasure, affectionate teasing, and an appetite for mutual discovery. She values a partner who can enjoy her enthusiasm without claiming ownership of it.',boundary='Her experiments, business choices, and free time are hers. She does not accept persistence after refusal as romantic determination.',memories=['A neighbor kept a struggling sapling alive through the dry summer and later credited Flora for it; she still thinks the neighbor did the harder work.','Her first flowers sold out at market, and she spent the profit on an impractical evening with friends.'],tasks=['water and inspect nursery stock','maintain propagation records','prepare orders and field visits','tend experimental plants','advise willing customers','close the glasshouse and plan trials'],anchors=[21,34,36],room='A cottage room with botanical sketches, dry seed envelopes, a few excellent books, and flowers arranged for pleasure rather than display.',ties=[(15,'business friendship','Flora and Inés turn growing experiments into market possibilities while arguing honestly about cost.'),(24,'neighbor friendship','Flora and Daisy share ambition, experiments, and an ability to laugh at attractive failures.'),(23,'outdoor friendship','Lena and Flora enjoy river outings and support each other’s wish to keep shared places accessible.')]),
26:dict(
 bio='Vera trained through study and laboratory apprenticeship before opening an independent assay office. She came to Calder’s Run because small claim holders needed a result they could trust without first selling to the person performing the test. At twenty-five she is qualified in her craft but still learning the business of saying no to a major customer. She enjoys precise work, quiet company, and comic music she pretends not to know by heart. Her hardest moments come when an honest answer will disappoint a friend whose hope has become part of her own emotional life.',look='Fair skin, cool gray eyes, dark brown hair cut to a practical length and pinned back, and a straight, thoughtful profile. Charcoal working dresses, clean white cuffs, a small lapel pin, and a dark teal coat outside work.',traits=['methodical','principled','reserved','loyal','dryly playful'],interests=['mineralogy','music','chess-like board games','hiking','careful cooking'],quirk='She checks whether a packet is properly labeled before discussing anything written on it.',belief='An answer has value because it can be checked, including when it is unwelcome.',tension='She values independence but wants enough security that a displeased customer cannot threaten it.',fear='That one careless error will justify every person who doubted her competence.',want='Maintain an independent laboratory and a circle of relationships where she is allowed to be uncertain.',obstacle='Equipment costs and dependence on repeat business from parties with a stake in the results.',secret='She has retained two conflicting sample seals and delayed a conclusion rather than risk implying a chain of custody she cannot establish.',voice='Precise, calm, and candid about limits. Her humor is dry enough to be missed by someone expecting solemnity.',lines=['I can test the sample you brought. Establishing where it came from is another part of the question.','Kit has decided I am too cautious. I have offered to put that finding in writing without charge.','An answer you prefer is not the same service as an answer you can trust.','I do not feel the need to prepare myself before you arrive. I am beginning to understand how much that means.'],romance='Patient attraction, dependable private meetings, intellectual play, and increasing warmth once honesty has survived a disagreement. She prefers clear invitations to grand gestures.',boundary='No altered result, confidential disclosure, or professional favor as proof of affection. She needs time to decide without pressure.',memories=['A mentor once praised her for refusing to interpret a sample without provenance; she expected criticism and remembered the lesson.','She learned a comic song for a friend’s supper and discovered she enjoyed being briefly ridiculous.'],tasks=['receive and document samples','conduct authorized laboratory work','compare records and custody seals','prepare qualified results','hold customer appointments','maintain equipment and accounts'],anchors=[39,24,42],room='A bluff lodging room with orderly books, a small game board, a music booklet tucked among technical notes, and a view of the evening ridge.',ties=[(29,'friendship under professional strain','Vera likes Kit and refuses to turn that affection into an optimistic result unsupported by the sample.'),(43,'working alliance','Ben brings wage and output concerns; Vera can support only what her actual testing and records establish.'),(17,'informal mentoring','Nell admires Vera’s method, and Vera encourages questions while respecting the limits of Nell’s apprenticeship.')]),
27:dict(
 bio='Sadie learned the road through work at a family coach stop, where a missed delivery could affect far more than the traveler making the complaint. At twenty-two she runs the station’s practical day and drives assigned routes. She is sociable, capable, and less reckless than her reputation suggests. She enjoys a good story but asks when the teller last checked it. Railway feeder work could secure her future, though its exclusivity would exclude independent carriers who helped keep the station alive. She wants to make a sound choice and dislikes discovering that loyalty cannot make all the options compatible.',look='Fair skin with a wind-browned tan, gray-green eyes, dark auburn hair in a practical braid, and a small pale scar at her jaw. Long brown duster, checked shirts, dark riding clothes, and a blue scarf kept for social evenings.',traits=['resourceful','sociable','bold','loyal','pragmatic'],interests=['driving','travel stories','cards','songs','cooking for a small company'],quirk='She asks whether someone wants the short version before telling a story that usually becomes the longer one.',belief='Reliability means telling people what they can actually expect, including a refusal.',tension='She believes in clear promises but has let different friends assume her next contract will favor them.',fear='Choosing a secure future and discovering she has made the place lonely.',want='Keep the station viable, travel on her own terms, and have a relationship that fits a mobile life.',obstacle='A promising railway contract requires ending some independent carriage.',secret='She has agreed to preliminary talks with Halden while allowing Eve and June to believe she has dismissed the offer.',voice='Brisk, story-rich, and warmly teasing. She speaks plainly about practical limits and slows down when acknowledging a personal mistake.',lines=['You can rest here or hear how the road is behaving. I recommend sitting down for either.','June says the return journey was uneventful. From June, that means she has edited it.','I should have told you I was considering the offer. I was hoping the decision would become easier before anyone knew it existed.','I have spent years making sure people can leave. It is a curious pleasure to want someone to come back.'],romance='Bold attraction, travel companionship, laughter, and freely negotiated commitment that accommodates work and distance. She values a person who can welcome her return without demanding that she never depart.',boundary='No dangerous journey, hidden cargo, or abandoned contract as a romantic test. Shared shelter never implies shared intimacy.',memories=['A stranded group once argued for hours and then cooperated beautifully when supper had to be made.','She remembers the first trip she took without carrying anyone else’s goods and wants another.'],tasks=['prepare scheduled coach departures','check animals and station supplies','drive assigned public routes','receive arrivals and freight','negotiate future carriage','close the station and plan the road'],anchors=[4,42,12],room='A private station room with maps, a good traveling coat, postcards and letters, and a supper table that folds away when she needs space.',ties=[(7,'professional friendship','Sadie trusts June with demanding work and expects the truth when a horse or consignment is uncertain.'),(30,'longstanding colleague','Eve and Sadie share route knowledge; an exclusive railway contract would strain their partnership.'),(38,'transport alliance','Nate and Sadie coordinate feasible connections and distrust timetables written to impress investors.')]),
}
